From 4ff495e74cb4cecf9952e503552b61eb64036e63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: floopflop <floop@tuta.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:03:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] etc: match udev change events, exit 0 from the sleep hook,
 meson 2.0-safe install_data

50-iptsd.rules matched ACTION=="add" only. udev rewrites a device's database
entry from the rules that match each event, so after a "change" event on the
hidraw node (a bare `udevadm trigger`, which the udisks2, nvme-cli and
qatlib-service package scriptlets run at every update of those packages) the
entry has neither the systemd tag nor SYSTEMD_WANTS. systemd (v247 and later,
which checks CURRENT_TAGS) then considers the device gone, BindsTo=%i.device
stops the running iptsd@ instance, and nothing starts it again until the next
"add" event: the touch device silently falls back to the firmware's native
mode. Match every event but "remove" so the tag and the Wants= survive;
systemd leaves an already active unit alone.

The system-sleep hook's only command is `[ "$1" = post ] && udevadm trigger`,
so the hook exits 1 in the "pre" phase and systemd-sleep logs a failure at
every suspend. Exit 0.

etc/meson.build passed the configure_file() outputs to install_data() by path
string; meson warns that this becomes a hard error in Meson 2.0. Pass the
returned file objects.
---
 etc/meson.build            | 7 ++-----
 etc/systemd-sleep/iptsd    | 6 +++++-
 etc/udev/50-iptsd.rules.in | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/etc/meson.build b/etc/meson.build
index dc7f56f..e7ea089 100644
--- a/etc/meson.build
+++ b/etc/meson.build
@@ -21,13 +21,13 @@ conf.set('bindir', bindir)
 conf.set('datadir', datadir)
 conf.set('sysconfdir', sysconfdir)
 
-configure_file(
+unit = configure_file(
 	input: 'systemd/iptsd@.service.in',
 	output: 'iptsd@.service',
 	configuration: conf,
 )
 
-configure_file(
+rule = configure_file(
 	input: 'udev/50-iptsd.rules.in',
 	output: '50-iptsd.rules',
 	configuration: conf,
@@ -48,9 +48,6 @@ if service_manager.contains('systemd')
 		udevdir = udev.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'udevdir')
 		rulesdir = join_paths(udevdir, 'rules.d')
 
-		unit = join_paths(meson.current_build_dir(), 'iptsd@.service')
-		rule = join_paths(meson.current_build_dir(), '50-iptsd.rules')
-
 		install_data(unit, install_dir: unitdir)
 		install_data(rule, install_dir: rulesdir)
 		install_data(
diff --git a/etc/systemd-sleep/iptsd b/etc/systemd-sleep/iptsd
index e5c593b..7dd3c4e 100644
--- a/etc/systemd-sleep/iptsd
+++ b/etc/systemd-sleep/iptsd
@@ -1,4 +1,8 @@
 #!/bin/bash
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
-[ "$1" = "post" ] && udevadm trigger --action=add --subsystem-match=hidraw
+# After resume, re-run the hidraw "add" rules so that iptsd@ is (re)started for the touch device.
+if [ "$1" = "post" ]; then
+	udevadm trigger --action=add --subsystem-match=hidraw
+fi
+exit 0
diff --git a/etc/udev/50-iptsd.rules.in b/etc/udev/50-iptsd.rules.in
index d7b1352..c4cd436 100644
--- a/etc/udev/50-iptsd.rules.in
+++ b/etc/udev/50-iptsd.rules.in
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ACTION=="add", TAG+="systemd", \
+SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ACTION!="remove", TAG+="systemd", \
 	PROGRAM="@bindir@/iptsd-check-device --quiet $env{DEVNAME}", \
 	PROGRAM="/bin/systemd-escape --path $env{DEVNAME}", \
 	ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="iptsd@$result.service"
-- 
2.56.0

